:'''Asta:''' This is...
:'''Dr. Ratio:''' A declaration of war and an announcement of what's to come &mdash; they have set their sights on you. The Legion's impact remains, and the Annihilation Gang is already paying a visit. It almost seems like this space station is more suited for the Path of Destruction than Erudition.
:'''Screwllum:''' This "Duke Inferno," Ifrit, is a lifeform that hails from Fetora &mdash; a world long since destroyed. His race, the ever-burning fire demons, regard Nanook as their emperor and savior, but the Aeon has never cast their gaze upon them.
:'''Dr. Ratio:''' A group of pitiful lunatics. I like Dr. Primitive's assessment of them: "The value Nanook sees in the Annihilation Gang is perhaps far less than what one might see in a child who deliberately broke a vase."
:'''Dr. Ratio:''' The fire demons have a cruel temper and instinctively ignite and destroy items. Ifrit is particularly evil and cruel, even among his kin. The Ever-Flame Mansion he heads is even the archenemy of the Jepella Brotherhood, despite both groups belonging to the Annihilation Gang.
:'''Asta:''' Jepella Brotherhood... I've heard that name somewhere...
:'''Screwllum:''' On the Stellaron Hunters' wanted posters, they stand accused of inciting the Jepella Rebellion &mdash; the uprising that caused the downfall of the Brotherhood.
:'''Dr. Ratio:''' The Jepella Palace crumbled in the scorching flames, and Ifrit's power has grown by the day ever since. Would you believe it to be merely a coincidence?
:'''Dr. Ratio:''' Something similar is about to happen here. Spontaneous combustion? For him, it's as routine as me finding fault in everything. The disappearance of researchers and the puppet were all part of the plan. And after that...
:'''Dr. Ratio:''' That video will soon circulate, and this station's fate? Flames, nothing but flames.
:'''Screwllum:''' The destruction of "trust."
:'''Dr. Ratio:''' I'm afraid more than trust will be destroyed here.
:'''Dr. Ratio:''' We need to start acting now if you want to survive. You &mdash; come with me.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Me?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Just me?
:'''Dr. Ratio:''' You have a superior strategy? Pray tell. Do we set the two of them loose, turning whispered fears into full-blown pandemonium?
:{{tx}}
{{Dialogue End}}

===Get Arlan's assistance{{subst:void|<!--200090113-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=continuance|location=Master Control Zone|update|You have temporarily exculpated yourself by the end of the interrogation, but Dr. Ratio specifically asked for you to go with him to Arlan to ask for help.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Arlan)
:'''Arlan:''' Not good... this is serious. The Security Department will do whatever we can to help you.
::'''Dr. Ratio:''' A list of the missing researchers and their details.
::'''Arlan:''' ...Sure, but the Security Department already combed through their backgrounds and personal relationships &mdash; we didn't find anything odd. The Annihilation Gang are a group of diehard thugs &mdash; they might be attacking indiscriminately...
::'''Dr. Ratio:''' A list of the missing researchers and their details.
::'''Arlan:''' O&mdash;Okay...
::'''Dr. Ratio:''' Take it. Remember these names &mdash; find a friend who's tuned in to the gossip around here and tell them you want to know the relationship between these people.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What do you have in mind?
::'''Dr. Ratio:''' I don't know. That depends on your friend.
::{{tx}}
:'''Arlan:''' I didn't really notice at first &mdash; Adler's difficult to get a hold of at the best of times...
::'''Arlan:''' ...but it's been a few system hours, and I still can't reach him. Even the surveillance cameras can't find any trace...
::'''Arlan:''' The last time I saw him was in the master control zone. He was with Wen Shiling from the Department of Implement Arts.

;(Talk to Asta)
:'''Asta:''' If we did that, we'd be at a disadvantage... I'll stay here and try to contain the news as best I can. Please investigate the issue quickly.

;(Talk to Screwllum)
:'''Screwllum:''' This "Duke Inferno," Ifrit, is a lifeform that hails from Fetora &mdash; a world long since destroyed. His race, the ever-burning fire demons, regard Nanook as their emperor and savior, but the Aeon has never cast their gaze upon them.
{{Dialogue End}}

